# * help command
# The help command is a documentation hub, dispatching on its first argument.

# ** 1. Bare help shows the quick reference card (like plain hledger).
$ hledger help
> /HLEDGER QUICK REFERENCE/

# ** 2. help commands shows the commands list.
$ hledger help commands
> /Commands \(including installed/

# ** 3. help usage shows general command-line usage.
$ hledger help usage
> /hledger's main command line interface/

# ** 4. help usage CMD shows that command's usage.
$ hledger help usage balance
> /^balance \[OPTIONS\]/

# ** 5. help manual TOPIC shows the manual.
$ hledger help manual journal
> /hledger User Manuals/

# ** 6. An unrecognised help argument is treated as a manual topic.
$ hledger help journal
> /hledger User Manuals/

# ** 7. help examples errors clearly when a command has no examples.
$ hledger help examples nosuchcommand
>2 /there are no examples for hledger-nosuchcommand/
>=1

# ** 8. help quickref shows the quick reference card.
$ hledger help quickref
> /HLEDGER QUICK REFERENCE/

# ** 9. help commands --builtin shows only built-in commands.
$ hledger help commands --builtin
> /Commands \(showing built-in/
